Our monitoring dashboard is running a query that seems inefficient. Can you look at this and suggest what might be wrong?

SELECT h.host_name, h.region, AVG(m.cpu_usage) as avg_cpu, MAX(m.memory_used) as peak_memory FROM hosts h JOIN metrics m ON h.host_id = m.host_id WHERE m.collected_at > NOW() - INTERVAL '7 days' GROUP BY h.host_id, h.host_name, h.region ORDER BY avg_cpu DESC LIMIT 20;

Query planner shows full table scan on metrics table

We're debugging a data export job that's hitting memory limits. Here's the query we're running — can you review it?

SELECT p.product_id, p.name, SUM(l.quantity) as total_sold FROM products p JOIN order_line_items l ON p.product_id = l.product_id WHERE p.category = 'electronics' GROUP BY p.product_id, p.name ORDER BY total_sold DESC;

OOM killed at 8GB on our ETL container
